# Plan: Replace Groq AI with NVIDIA NIM (Free Cloud Models)

## Context
The Kippo🌸 ticketing platform currently uses Groq AI (`groq-sdk`) for its admin AI assistant with tool/function calling to query and modify the database. The goal is to replace this with NVIDIA NIM's free cloud API, which is OpenAI-compatible and supports 100+ models including Llama with tool calling.

## Key Differences
| | Groq | NVIDIA NIM |
|---|---|---|
| SDK | `groq-sdk` | `openai` (OpenAI-compatible) |
| Base URL | `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1` | `https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1` |
| API Key Env | `GROQ_API_KEY` (`gsk_...`) | `NVIDIA_API_KEY` (`nvapi-...`) |
| Model | `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` | `meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct` |
| Free Tier | Yes | Yes (1,000-5,000 credits, never expire) |
| Tool Calling | Yes | Yes (OpenAI format) |

## Steps

### 1. Replace `groq-sdk` with `openai` in `package.json`
- Remove `"groq-sdk": "^1.3.0"` from dependencies
- Add `"openai": "^4.x"` to dependencies
- Run `npm install`

### 2. Rewrite `src/lib/ai/groq.ts` → `src/lib/ai/nvidia.ts`
- Import `OpenAI` from `openai` instead of `Groq` from `groq-sdk`
- Initialize client with `baseURL: "https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1"` and `apiKey: process.env.NVIDIA_API_KEY`
- Update model names:
  - Primary call: `"meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct"` (supports tool calling)
  - Follow-up call: `"meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct"` (same model for consistency)
- Keep all tool definitions, system prompt, and `chatWithAgent()` function signature identical
- Update internal variable names from `groq`/`groqClient` to `client`

### 3. Update `src/app/api/ai/chat/route.ts`
- Change import from `@/lib/ai/groq` to `@/lib/ai/nvidia`

### 4. Update `src/app/kicheleboyz/ai/page.tsx`
- Change "Groq AI" badge text to "NVIDIA AI" (line 159)

### 5. Update `SETUP.md`
- Replace `GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...` with `NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...`

### 6. Delete old `src/lib/ai/groq.ts` file

## Files to Modify
- `package.json` — swap dependencies
- `src/lib/ai/groq.ts` — rewrite as `src/lib/ai/nvidia.ts`
- `src/app/api/ai/chat/route.ts` — update import
- `src/app/kicheleboyz/ai/page.tsx` — update badge text
- `SETUP.md` — update env var docs

## Verification
- `npm run build` should succeed with no TypeScript errors
- `npm run lint` should pass
- The AI assistant at `/kicheleboyz/ai` should work with the NVIDIA NIM endpoint
